{
 "id": "2026-11-06-hera-reaches-didymos",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {"id": "hook", "text": "We hit an asteroid on purpose. Europe's probe just arrived to inspect it."},
  {"id": "f1", "text": "The European Space Agency says its Hera spacecraft reached the Didymos asteroid pair this week, after launching in October twenty twenty-four. In September twenty twenty-two, NASA's DART probe slammed into Dimorphos, the small moon of Didymos."},
  {"id": "f2", "text": "Telescopes on Earth showed the result. Dimorphos now circles its parent about thirty-three minutes faster. But nobody has seen the impact scar up close. Hera carries cameras and instruments to measure the moon's mass, shape and crater."},
  {"id": "f3", "text": "ESA says Hera will also release two small CubeSats, named Milani and Juventas. Full-resolution images of both asteroids are due on November twenty-fifth. Until then, how the impact reshaped Dimorphos remains unknown."},
  {"id": "cta", "text": "Will Hera's images show a clear crater? Yes or no?"}
 ],
